{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790193305,"nonce":"/lpWu3Ia6EThQVTPaRR/E+lDwHc=","message":"Final shape 2026-09-23 (Luis), doc/design/cli-convention.md: `get ID` (whole document, replaces show; no per-field getter), `set ID FIELDS` / `add ID ITEMS` / `remove ID ITEMS` each take a JSON object and commit one operation per key of one type (SetField, AddValue, RemoveValue), which is the dag's own write unit, a commit = list of ops. RFC 6902 `patch` is dropped: a second grammar over the same three ops that bakes the read shape's paths into the write API; if a mixed commit ever needs a consumer, `patch ID OPS` in the ops' wire shape is the superset. `comment new ISSUE_ID BODY|-` and `comment edit COMMENT_ID BODY|-` only; no comment list or show (get prints comments). `archive ID` is first class on every tree. `log ID`, `rm ID` (local). Default list program is mine+unarchived; `.` is everything.","files":null}]}